{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>who dwells with them in the midst of their impurity.</b> Even though they are impure, the Shekhinah is among them. And this was the view of R. Yehudah, of blessed memory, in tractate Sukkah, who used to say that one may roof a sukkah with something that receives impurity, and he said so on account of this verse, even though the halakhah does not follow him. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded (Genesis 27): ״וירח את ריח בגדיו״ — even the smell of traitors (בוגדיו). And they further expounded (Psalms 68): ״עלית למרום״ etc. — even rebels dwell with the Elohim of YHWH (לשכן יה אלהים); even if there are rebels and transgressors among them, the Shekhinah is among them. And they further expounded (Malachi 2): ״כי שנא שלח אמר ה׳ אלהי ישראל״ — throughout the book of Malachi He mentioned ״צבאות,״ but here ״אלהי ישראל״; rather, even though you are hated and sent away, I am your Elohim — therefore He mentioned ״אלהי ישראל.״ And in the Midrash: ״who dwells with them in the midst of their impurity״ — even though Israel is in exile and they are not pure in their exile, the Shekhinah dwells with them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:58.887124741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}